From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:20:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 303/306] nb/intel/haswell/native_raminit: Shorten tWRRD
 between ranks as the MRC does

After a write to one rank the controller waits tWRRD_dr or tWRRD_dd
clocks before a read from another rank. refresh_timings() sets both to
the sum of the JEDEC times; on a ThinkPad W541 with four dual-rank
DIMMs that is 4, where mrc.bin ends at 3.

A scan for the shortest value that passes cannot find it: on this
controller the turnaround test of the REUT passes down to 0 (measured
in v1.7.0-rc3 and rc4), the controller keeping a spacing of its own.
The turnaround step of the MRC in the Lenovo firmware of the W541 does
not scan: it tries the JEDEC value minus one clock and keeps it if the
turnaround test passes with the read and write eyes squeezed, the read
and write timing moved by 7 PI ticks and the read and write voltage by
7 Vref steps, to each side, one at a time.

Add HASWELL_NRI_TURNAROUND, which does that after the round trip step.
A note of the result goes to the summary. Not run in the training that
is done again after a failure.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I7cee625f9e04fd8cba2d3fd851f14e13d757e07e
